      {
        "id": "s6",
        "kind": "explain",
        "title": "Equations in disguise",
        "body": "$2y = 6x + 8$ and $3x - y + 4 = 0$ are straight lines too. Rearrange to $y = mx + c$ before reading off the gradient: both become $y = 3x + 4$.\n\nExam questions also ask for the form $ax + by + c = 0$ with integer $a$, $b$, $c$: multiply through to clear fractions, then move everything to one side.",
        "visuals": [
          {
            "type": "worked-example",
            "problem": "Rearrange $3y - 6x = 12$",
            "steps": [
              {
                "text": "$3y = 6x + 12$"
              },
              {
                "text": "$y = 2x + 4$"
              },
              {
                "text": "Gradient 2, intercept 4"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "check": {
          "id": "c6",
          "type": "short-text",
          "prompt": "Write $2y = 8x - 6$ in the form $y = mx + c$.",
          "marks": 1,
