      "gradeBand": "8-9",
      "skill": "equation in the form ax + by + c = 0",
      "calculator": "either",
      "tags": [],
      "solution": "Gradient $= \\dfrac{-3 - 9}{4 - (-2)} = \\dfrac{-12}{6} = -2$. Then $9 = -2(-2) + c$, so $c = 5$ and $y = -2x + 5$. Rearranged: $2x + y - 5 = 0$.",
      "markScheme": [
        {
